From 5252286b5961c10c749dfa16d48d71cfe8d6aa2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
Date: Tue, 21 Jul 2026 07:43:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 83/90] usb: dwc3: Do not connect the gadget while no cable is
 present

usb_add_gadget() starts out assuming VBUS is present and binds any
gadget driver that was waiting, so the connect happens inside
dwc3_gadget_init(), before dwc3 has any way to say there is no cable.
With the USB3 PHY powered down while disconnected, that runs the
endpoint setup against a PHY that is off:

  dwc3 fe800000.usb: request 000000002e1b5f5e was not queued to ep0out
  udc fe800000.usb: failed to start adbd: -524
  configfs-gadget.adbd gadget.2: probe with driver configfs-gadget.adbd
      failed with error -524

The gadget driver is then unbound for good, so the port stays dead until
userspace sets it up again. It shows up after a host to device role
change with nothing plugged in, which is where the gadget is registered
while disconnected.

Remember the request instead and leave the pullup to the connection
state, which __dwc3_set_mode() already reports through
usb_udc_vbus_handler().

Signed-off-by: Ondrej Jirman <megi@xff.cz>
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
index 45b468b4c9b5..88792b22efc1 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc3/gadget.c
@@ -2797,6 +2797,20 @@ static int dwc3_gadget_pullup(struct usb_gadget *g, int is_on)
 
 	dwc->softconnect = is_on;
 
+	/*
+	 * The UDC core connects as soon as a gadget driver binds, because it
+	 * assumes VBUS is present until told otherwise, and it can only be
+	 * told once the gadget is registered. On a port that powers its PHYs
+	 * down while nothing is plugged in, that would run the endpoint setup
+	 * against a PHY that is off and fail the bind.
+	 *
+	 * Record the request and let the connection state drive it instead.
+	 * __dwc3_set_mode() reports that state, so the pullup follows the
+	 * cable either way.
+	 */
+	if (is_on && dwc->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG && !dwc->current_dr_connected)
+		return 0;
+
 	/*
 	 * Avoid issuing a runtime resume if the device is already in the
 	 * suspended state during gadget disconnect.  DWC3 gadget was already
